    "title": "Two killed, another injured in Westinghouse Blvd crash - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Doug Coats ,\n5 hours ago\nCHARLOTTE, N.C. (QUEEN CITY NEWS) — Two people are dead from a crash in southwest Charlotte Wednesday evening, Medic officials say.\nAccording to local authorities, the crash was reported around 6:10 p.m. in the 1600 block of Westinghouse Boulevard. Another victim was taken to the hospital with life-threatening injuries, Medic says.\nThe road was closed for several hours east of South Tryon.\nCharlotte-Mecklenburg Police and Charlotte Fire also responded to the scene.\nHow the crash occurred is unknown at this time.\nThis is a Developing Story . Check back for updates\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to Queen City News.",
    "summary": "CHARLOTTE, N.C. (QUEEN CITY NEWS) — Two people are dead from a crash in southwest Charlotte Wednesday evening, Medic officials say. According to local authorities, the crash was reported around 6:10 p.m. in the 1600 block of Westinghouse Boulevard. The road was closed for several hours east of South Tryon. Charlotte-Mecklenburg Police and Charlotte Fire also responded to the scene. Check back for updates Copyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved.",
